     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** the maximum is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Many references use 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day as the ceiling.\n- **Extended-release:** the maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended orders:\n\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and give a short note on why, such as a protocol or special circumstance. I can then enter it with that note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
